From 90a120c163a330a69a0ef8978b97e813e8330d1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:56:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add zero-knowledge Password Locker for admins

Per-admin vault for passwords, API/secret keys and secure notes:
- Browser derives keys from the master password with Argon2id
  (64 MiB, 3 passes) and HKDF; items sealed with AES-256-GCM under a
  random data key. Server never sees the master password or plaintext.
- Server re-wraps every ciphertext with AES-256-GCM (VAULT_SERVER_KEY,
  bound to the vault id) and stores only an scrypt hash of the derived
  auth key.
- Short-lived HMAC-signed vault session cookie, revoked on lock or
  master password change; escalating lockout after 5 failed unlocks.
- UI: setup/unlock, search and filters, reveal/copy with 30s clipboard
  clear, password generator, strength meter, 5-minute idle auto-lock,
  change master password, and delete-vault for forgotten passwords.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YRuSBK59XDedyAY1FcRsm4
